# protobuf 4.25.9 DoS (python: recursive parsing) in ja4proxy-test — the CI-only,
# profile-gated tooling image (never deployed; skipped by 'make build'). No fix
# available: protobuf 5.29.6 needs semgrep>=1.137, whose mcp==1.23.3 pin would
# reintroduce CVE-2025-66416 (see phase-800 note in requirements.txt). protobuf
# there is only exercised by semgrep/OTEL tooling on trusted repo content.
# Re-review at expiry: check for a semgrep release with OTEL>=1.37 AND mcp>=1.28.
CVE-2026-0994 exp:2026-07-29

# GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf: gRPC-Go xDS RBAC and HTTP/2 Vulnerabilities (fixed in
# grpc-go v1.82.1). Newly disclosed/indexed; as of this review no upstream
# release of prometheus (v3.13.1, latest), alertmanager (v0.33.1, latest),
# grafana (13.0.4-ubuntu, latest — verified still on v1.80.0), loki (3.7.4,
# latest — verified still on v1.81.1), or promtail (v3.6.11, latest) has
# picked up the fix yet.
# Why not exploitable here: the vulnerable code paths are gRPC's xDS RBAC
# filter and an HTTP/2 handling flaw used by Envoy-style xDS control planes.
# None of these five images run as xDS servers or accept untrusted gRPC/xDS
# input in our deployment — they're monitoring/logging tools sitting behind
# the proxy, reachable only from trusted internal callers.
GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf exp:2026-07-29
